        <type>std::string</type>
        <definition>virtual std::string SgAsmScalarType::toString</definition>
        <argsstring>() const override</argsstring>
        <name>toString</name>
        <reimplements refid="classSgAsmType_1a2919978a83bc7d59f0ac3abf544aa40a">toString</reimplements>
        <reimplementedby refid="classSgAsmPointerType_1a92f4d374ef86fd69d2734234b270fd2e">toString</reimplementedby>
        <reimplementedby refid="classSgAsmIntegerType_1a4a676dd638172e5e8150aa9cfb801f1f">toString</reimplementedby>
        <reimplementedby refid="classSgAsmFloatType_1a64e7dcbff12ae90e12d70d2db4bbfc33">toString</reimplementedby>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Convert a type to a string.</para><para>The output is intended mostly for debugging since it contains more details than what would be typically useful. For instance, instead of the word &quot;double&quot;, this will probably print all the details about where the various floating-point fields are located, how the exponent field works, etc. </para>        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="/home/liao6/workspace/rose-github/src/AstNodes/BinaryAnalysis/SgAsmScalarType.h" line="44" column="1"/>
